  "stem": "\\[3x + 4y = 10\\] \\[5x - 2y = 34\\] If \\((x, y)\\) is the solution to the system of equations above, what is the value of \\(x + y\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "4"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Multiply the second equation by 2: \\(10x - 4y = 68\\).",
    "Add it to the first equation: \\(13x = 78\\), so \\(x = 6\\).",
    "Then \\(3(6) + 4y = 10\\) gives \\(y = -2\\), so \\(x + y = 4\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x, y = symbols('x y')\nsol = solve([3*x + 4*y - 10, 5*x - 2*y - 34], [x, y])\nassert sol == {x: 6, y: -2}\nassert [Rational(a) for a in spr_answers] == [sol[x] + sol[y]]",
